{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS001262","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Endpoint fidelity: per the trait-label guidance, phenotyping_reported is the primary endpoint field. PGS001262 uses a direct diagnosis-style endpoint (“Vascular/heart problems diagnosed by doctor Angina”) that maps cleanly to angina pectoris, whereas PGS001261 is explicitly time-to-event (a warning signal unless it has clearly stronger PRS-only evidence, which it does not here).

Performance evidence: per the performance-metrics guidance, PRS-only metrics are the most comparable cross-model signal. PGS001262 reports PRS AUROC (no covariates)=0.58683 and PRS R2 (no covariates)=0.01304, slightly stronger than PGS001260 and PGS001261, and it also has the largest incremental AUROC (0.0098). Several other candidates lack PRS-only metrics (PGS000703 reports only full-model AUROC ~0.593; the 2024 Commun Biol scores report only OR with unknown covariates; the 2024 MVP method-comparison scores report full-model C-index without isolating PRS-only contribution), making them less reliable for selection despite sometimes higher full-model discrimination.

Heritability sanity-check: local EUR LDSC records for ICD10 I20 Angina pectoris show observed h2 ~0.012–0.016 (liability h2 ~0.09–0.19). The PRS-only R2 for PGS001262 (~0.013) is in a plausible range relative to these h2 records, supporting that the reported PRS-only signal is not obviously inconsistent with trait genetic architecture."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS000448","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"All candidates are direct matches for the target trait (basal cell carcinoma) by trait_reported/trait_efo, so endpoint fidelity is acceptable across the list (per the general comparison procedure in the prs_model_evaluator skill_overview). None report PRS-only AUROC/R2; per prs_model_evaluator performance_metrics guidance, full-model AUROC is not a reliable cross-model ranking metric when PRS-only metrics are absent, so effect sizes and other supportive signals under comparable covariates should drive selection.

Among the Cancer PRSweb sibling models (Am J Hum Genet, 2020-12-15) evaluated in Europeans with basic covariates (age, sex, batch, PCs 1–4), PGS000448 (lassosum; 183 variants) has the strongest per-SD effect size (OR 1.411, 95% CI 1.335–1.491) and the strongest top-1% vs rest enrichment (OR 2.93, 95% CI 2.03–4.25), with a similar full-model AUROC (0.587) to nearby siblings—making it the best-supported candidate in this fixed set. Publication context does not overturn this: the PRSweb/Cancer PRSweb papers are disease-focused cross-cancer repositories with direct endpoint evaluation (prs_model_evaluator publication_context notes titles/journals are mainly for study-type detection, not performance ranking).

Heritability sanity-check (get_heritability_records, EUR LDSC): basal cell carcinoma shows low observed-scale h2 (~0.010–0.013) but higher liability-scale h2 (~0.14–0.21) in UKB self-report records, consistent with expecting only modest-to-moderate discrimination and reinforcing that we should not over-interpret small full-model AUROC differences; the observed OR magnitudes for PGS000448 are plausible under this ceiling."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS000997","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Trait/endpoint alignment (prs_model_evaluator skill_overview + trait_labels): the target is generic “diverticular disease”. PGS000997 has trait_efo “diverticular disease” and phenotyping_reported “TTE diverticular disease of intestine”, which is still a direct diagnosis endpoint but with a time-to-event framing (a mild warning signal, not a disqualifier). PGS000996 is also aligned but is a broader composite label “Diverticular disease/diverticulitis”. PGS004474/PGS004544 are ICD10 K57 diverticular disease of intestine (direct match), and PGS004614 is also direct.

Comparable performance evidence (prs_model_evaluator performance_metrics): prioritize PRS-comparable metrics (PGS-only AUROC/R²) over full-model AUROC that can be covariate-driven. Only PGS000996 and PGS000997 report explicit PGS-only metrics; among them PGS000997 is materially stronger (PGS-only AUROC 0.591 vs 0.552; PGS-only R² 0.0178 vs 0.0037) with similar basic covariates (age, sex, array, PCs) and same UKB snpnet study family, making the comparison fair. PGS004614 reports only full-model AUROC (0.76) and includes family history in covariates, which reduces comparability to standalone PRS performance. PGS004474/PGS004544 report only per-SD ORs (~1.31–1.32), which suggests moderate signal but is less directly comparable than PGS-only AUROC/R² here.

Heritability sanity check (get_heritability_records): UKB-matched diverticular disease endpoints show observed h2 roughly ~0.01–0.03 (with liability h2 ~0.12–0.25 for K57/self-reported diverticular disease/diverticulitis). PGS000997’s PGS-only R² of 0.0178 is plausible relative to these h2 records (i.e., not implausibly high), supporting it as a credible higher-signal choice versus PGS000996 within the candidates."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS000083","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Trait/endpoint alignment (prs_model_evaluator trait-label guidance): the target is “pancreatic carcinoma,” and PGS000083 is a coherent direct match across fields—trait_reported pancreatic cancer, trait_efo exocrine pancreatic carcinoma, and phenotyping_reported incident pancreatic cancer—where phenotyping_reported is the primary endpoint-fidelity signal. PGS002264 targets pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (a carcinoma subtype) but its reported performance is embedded in a clinically packaged model (diabetes onset categories, waist circumference, family history/clinical risk), which reduces comparability to standalone PRS quality per the performance-metrics guidance.

Performance evidence (prs_model_evaluator performance-metrics guidance): no candidate provides an explicit PGS-only AUROC/R2, so full-model AUROC must be interpreted cautiously and covariate sets matter. PGS000083 has supportive discrimination evidence (full-model AUROC 0.745; C-index ~0.742) plus a near-strong per-SD effect size (HR 1.49) in a very large European validation (n=391,491). Competing UKB PRSweb/UKB-style models (PGS000385/000386/004693) show materially lower AUROCs (~0.54–0.59), and PGS000725 is also lower (0.639).

Heritability sanity-check (EUR): local records for pancreatic cancer show modest SNP-heritability (h2≈0.0568; liability h2≈0.0893). This supports expecting only moderate standalone PRS performance and reinforces not over-weighting covariate-boosted AUROCs; within that constraint, PGS000083’s combination of direct endpoint fidelity, large validation, and moderate-to-strong HR signal makes it the best-supported choice from the fixed candidate list."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS000611","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Phenotype/endpoint fidelity is acceptable across the pool: candidates consistently target bladder cancer / urinary bladder carcinoma, with phenotyping_reported entries like “Cancer of bladder”, “Bladder cancer”, and “Incident bladder cancer”, which are direct diagnosis endpoints for the target trait (read_skill_section: trait_labels). Per the evaluator framework, once endpoint alignment is broadly satisfied, prioritize comparable PRS evidence over covariate-boosted full-model discrimination, and weigh covariate cleanliness and study context (read_skill_section: skill_overview; performance_metrics).

PGS000071 and PGS000782 report very high full-model AUROC (~0.80) but include substantial non-genetic risk factors (smoking variables and BMI), so those AUROCs are not strong evidence of standalone PRS quality. The PRSweb (Am J Hum Genet) bladder scores use basic covariates (age/sex/batch/PCs) and provide more PRS-informative signals (Nagelkerke R² and tail ORs). Within that family, PGS000611 (GWAS Hits; 13 variants; UKB-based; eval n=13,530) has the strongest combined evidence: AUROC 0.567, Nagelkerke R² 0.0114, and a strong tail effect (OR top 1% vs rest 2.66, CI 1.79–3.93), while other PRSweb bladder scores show lower AUROC/R² and/or weaker/unstable tail ORs.

Heritability lookup for “urinary bladder cancer” in local EUR records shows very low observed h2 for self-reported bladder cancer (h2 ~0.0007–0.0011; liability h2 ~0.048–0.054), supporting cautious expectations for PRS-explained variance and reinforcing that extremely high full-model AUROC values are likely driven by covariates rather than genetic score signal (get_heritability_records)."}
